# No destructive database changes on deploy

User word banks, learned words, profiles, and progress are live production data.

## Never without an explicit user request in this conversation

- `DELETE` / `TRUNCATE` / wipe migrations (e.g. reset learned words)
- `supabase db push` (or equivalent) when pending migrations include destructive SQL
- Repairing migration history in a way that re-applies destructive scripts
- Any “clear all users’ X” SQL run against the linked/remote project

## On publish / deploy

- Deploy edge **functions** only unless the user explicitly asks to apply DB migrations.
- Before any `db push`, read pending migration SQL. If any statement deletes or resets user rows, **stop and ask** — do not apply.
- Prefer schema-additive migrations (`CREATE`, `ALTER … ADD`, new policies). Put one-off data wipes in a separately named file and never auto-run them.

## If a reset is actually needed

Ask first, name the tables/rows affected, and wait for a clear yes. “Publish the site” is not permission to wipe user data.
